  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the required files:\n\n1. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`** \u2014 contains the root cause: `_extract_tar_dir()` does `tar._ansible_normalized_cache[dirname]` instead of `tar.getmember(dirname)`, and the cache is built as `{m.name.removesuffix(os.path.sep): m for m in collection_tar.getmembers()}` right before the extraction loop, explicitly commented as a workaround for CPython bug `bugs.python.org/issue47231`, deprecated for py3.11/core_version 2.18.\n2. **`test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py`** \u2014 existing unit test exercising `_extract_tar_dir` via a fully mocked `_ansible_normalized_cache`, showing the established test pattern and confirming a lookup miss raises `AnsibleError(\"Unable to extract...\")`.\n3. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/concrete_artifact_manager.py`** \u2014 the sibling tar-handling module that correctly uses stdlib `collection_tar.getmember(MANIFEST_FILENAME)` for member lookup (contrast case) and defines `_tarfile_extract`.\n4. **`changelogs/fragments/a-g-col-install-directory-with-trailing-sep.yml`** \u2014 changelog fragment documenting the original trailing-separator bugfix this cache was tied to.",
